From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:21:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: let an L2 bridge flow carry 512
 connections

In bridge mode the whole house is one L2 flow per direction, and the
cap on its subflows is how many connections the PPE carries for it.
With 256, after 999-81 and 42 h of normal use on the XR500v, the
parents were still full about 725 times an hour (l2_subflow_full),
and each time a new connection went through the CPU until a place
was freed; the download parent held 195 of its 256 subflows on a quiet
afternoon.

Raised to 512 at run time (ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows) for 2.4 h of the
same use: l2_subflow_full stayed at 0 and the upload parent went
above 256 within seconds. softirq time was 1.7 % over those afternoon
hours (the 42 h average with 256, nights included, was 1.0 %): the
longer walk of rx_check over the flows of a packet without one does
not show at these rates.

Make 512 the default; the parameter keeps its 16..1024 range.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -3229,10 +3229,11 @@ static unsigned long airoha_ppe_v1_flow_
 /*
  * In bridge mode all the traffic of the house is a single MAC pair per
  * direction, so the cap on the subflows of an L2 flow is how many of its
- * connections the PPE carries. It is small because rx_check walks every flow
- * for each packet that has none: do not raise the default before that
- * changes. A subflow that carries nothing must then leave soon. Subflows
- * are freed when their parent is full, at most once a second:
+ * connections the PPE carries. rx_check walks every flow for each packet that
+ * has none, so the cap also bounds that walk; on the XR500v 512 stopped the
+ * parents from filling up with softirq time still under 2 %. A subflow that
+ * carries nothing must still leave soon. Subflows are freed when their parent
+ * is full, at most once a second:
  *
  *  - one that owns a hardware entry, after ppe_v1_l2_idle seconds without
  *    traffic. The PPE itself unbinds an entry that was idle for 15 s, so
@@ -3242,11 +3243,11 @@ static unsigned long airoha_ppe_v1_flow_
  *    unbound is a single packet, such as a port scan from the Internet or a
  *    DNS query, and each of those took a place for the full idle time.
  */
-static unsigned int airoha_ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows = 256;
+static unsigned int airoha_ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows = 512;
 module_param_named(ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows, airoha_ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows,
 		   uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(ppe_v1_l2_max_subflows,
-		 "Hardware subflows one L2 bridge flow may have, 16 to 1024 (default: 256)");
+		 "Hardware subflows one L2 bridge flow may have, 16 to 1024 (default: 512)");
 
 static unsigned int airoha_ppe_v1_l2_idle = 20;
 module_param_named(ppe_v1_l2_idle, airoha_ppe_v1_l2_idle, uint, 0644);
